{"uid":"839b622febf4409c","name":"test_review_findings_unusable_pauses_and_never_archives_or_cures","fullName":"tests.test_contract_ladder#test_review_findings_unusable_pauses_and_never_archives_or_cures","historyId":"ed1ad9935e0b59f43cb34e9d264af250","time":{"start":1791889957976,"stop":1791889958052,"duration":76},"description":"Task 011 (PRD requirement C.2, #219): the pause edge this task adds\n    (`review -> paused` on `review_findings_unusable`), driven through a\n    real `_step_review()` over each of the THREE named shapes requirement\n    C draws the flag from (`LoopSupervisor._review_contract_ladder`'s own\n    `findings_channel_unusable_reply`): a present-but-invalid (truncated)\n    sidecar, a `verified` claim contradicting a blocking finding, and a\n    curable finding with no `cured_when`. Every shape must leave the SAME\n    fingerprint: `state: \"paused\"` with `pauseReason: \"review_findings_\n    unusable\"`, no `approaches/NN/` directory written, no composite PRD,\n    the approach counter unchanged, and no cure pass opened (neither\n    `curePasses` on status.json nor an `approach.cure_pass` event) --\n    exactly the consequences `test_ladder_exhaustion_holds_for_an_operator_\n    and_never_archives` above already pins for the sibling edge.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 011 (PRD requirement C.2, #219): the pause edge this task adds<br />\n(<code>review -&gt; paused</code> on <code>review_findings_unusable</code>), driven through a<br />\nreal <code>_step_review()</code> over each of the THREE named shapes requirement<br />\nC draws the flag from (<code>LoopSupervisor._review_contract_ladder</code>'s own<br />\n<code>findings_channel_unusable_reply</code>): a present-but-invalid (truncated)<br />\nsidecar, a <code>verified</code> claim contradicting a blocking finding, and a<br />\ncurable finding with no <code>cured_when</code>. Every shape must leave the SAME<br />\nfingerprint: <code>state: &quot;paused&quot;</code> with <code>pauseReason